raylib-games classics, upstream raysan5/raylib-games commit
318688c759eaf391b36b9f893355c038fcf56419, under the zlib license.

The repository LICENSE and classics/LICENSE are installed unchanged as LICENSE
and CLASSICS-LICENSE. The game sources retain their original copyright notices:
Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5), and, for platformer, Agnis "NeZvers" (@nezvers)
and Ramon Santamaria. The upstream platformer source contains the coauthor's
full name in its original encoding.

This is a Pyxis build of the twelve classics source files. No upstream source
is modified. The recipe supplies only static SDK build rules and native bundle
manifests. Games retain their upstream rules, input, drawing and frame pacing.
All visuals are generated; no external game assets or audio are distributed.
Other raylib-games collections, upstream binaries and screenshots are omitted.

The executables statically link the separately built raylib/rlsw and SDL2.
Public packages must retain their complete notices and provenance, together
with those of the SDK runtime closure.
